- **src/services/contentstack.ts** (`options`): This is the Contentstack SDK initialization config where live_preview settings must be injected. The Stack is created from these options (line 91), and all content queries (getEntry, getSingleEntry, ContentstackFactory) flow through this Stack instance. Contentstack's Live Preview feature requires adding a live_preview config block to the Stack initialization options, making this the primary attachment point for the new preview capability.
  - **Minimal fix:** Add a live_preview config block to the options object (after line 88, before the closing brace on line 89). The block should read CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST and CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN from process.env and, when present, set live_preview: { enable: true, host: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST, preview_token: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN }. Also add CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST and CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN to the destructured env vars at lines 23-36. This is the minimal change — Contentstack's SDK natively supports live_preview in the Stack config; no new fetching logic is needed. The getEntry/getSingleEntry functions will automatically receive draft content when preview parameters are present in the request context.

